@nsobid-FA3897E0FADDD49C69ED00F23E705B3E

# Splatoon 2 1.1.0 QA Build 2 - 4096x4096 shadow resolution

@flag print_values
@flag offset_shift 0x100

// Forces the sun/cascade depth-shadow map to 4096x4096 (stock default 1024x1024).
// Every frame gsys::ModelSceneShadow::drawDepthShadow reads the two shadow-map
// dimensions out of gsys::ModelSceneConfig (the depth_shadow_tex_width /
// depth_shadow_tex_height env parameters), multiplies them by the viewport ratio,
// clamps the result so it can never EXCEED the configured value, and hands that to
// agl::sdw::ShadowMap::setSize. That clamp is why raising the render resolution on
// its own leaves shadows at their original size. These two lines replace the config
// reads with immediates, so the shadow map is pinned to a fixed size instead.
//
// MEMORY: the shadow map is allocated per frame from the same fixed
// DynamicTextureAllocator pool as the post-effect buffers, and it grows with the
// SQUARE of this number (4096x4096 is 16x the texels of stock 1024x1024).
// Pair this with one of the [WxH] resolution mods, which enlarge that pool. If the
// game aborts in agl::utl::DynamicTextureAllocator::alloc_ ("alloc failed ... free
// size"), the pool is too small for this shadow size at that resolution -- step down
// a shadow size or up a resolution mod.

@enabled
013E9A2C 09008252
013E9A30 08008252
@stop

// Shadow-map sizing reverse-engineered against the gsys/agl engine
// (gsys::ModelSceneShadow::drawDepthShadow -> agl::sdw::ShadowMap::setSize).
//
// https://github.com/RAMDRAGONS/switch-visuen-mods
